Fixed the sibling race: `deliver!` had the same read-then-mutate gap as `accept-slot!` — it read `(:phase @state)` to decide whether to queue, but `accept-slot!` could flip the phase and replay the queue in the gap before the queuing `swap!` ran, silently losing the frame into a queue nobody would ever replay again. Made the phase-check and queue-mutation one atomic `swap!` (mirroring the fix from the previous turn), with a volatile carrying the winning branch's decision back out for the deposit/protocol-failure side effect. JVM (2277/183258/0, 3 clean runs) and Node (2183/49888/0, 2 clean runs) lanes are green; Dart is compiling in the background — I'll report its result once it completes.
